  message: "DONE 2026-09-06 (PR #794). The second leg of WI-lutuh's order, shipped as pre-registered in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jsleg_completeness_09062026/PLAN.md.\n\nINSTRUMENT: probe.js (node v20.19.6; exports one level deep incl. prototype methods; function source scanned for binding reach -- internalBinding, binding., [kHandle], fd, native -- and I/O surface names; cross-referenced with javascript.yaml as loaded; NEVER grants) and probe_fs.js (per-export binding calls for direction). probe_v0.out / probe_fs.out are the record.\n\nSHIPPED (javascript.yaml): 76 rows added -- fs: open/openSync (dual fs_read+fs_write, builtins.open shape; no js io_mode stamp so an unstamped open keeps fs_read), read/readSync/readv/readvSync, fstat/fstatSync, statfs/statfsSync, opendir/opendirSync, openAsBlob, exists, createReadStream, watch/watchFile (fs_read); write/writeSync/writev/writevSync, fchmod/fchown/fdatasync/fsync/ftruncate/futimes (+Sync), lchown, lutimes, link, symlink, truncate, utimes, mkdtemp, rm, cp (+Sync) (fs_write); fs.promises: open, opendir, statfs, watch (fs_read); cp, lchmod, lchown, link, lutimes, mkdtemp, symlink, truncate, utimes, open (fs_write); process: getuid/geteuid/getgid/getegid/getgroups/cpuUsage/memoryUsage/resourceUsage/constrainedMemory/availableMemory/umask + attributes pid/ppid/execPath/title/versions/release (host_info_read), openStdin (ipc_recv), chdir (env_write, os.chdir precedent), dlopen (fs_read). 7 rows DELETED: path.* (INV-nular F7, WI-jojaf) and, in python.yaml, os.path.abspath + posixpath.abspath. GRANTS (10, dated 2026-09-06, each citing its probe verdict): path, url, zlib, timers/promises, stream/promises, crypto (python entropy precedent, pinned by test), fs, fs/promises, fs.promises, process. WITHHELD with the reason in the yaml: readline (stream argument decides, no js stamp), http (new http.Server()/Agent() not keyed); net/dns/child_process/os/https/dgram/tls not audited. Catalogue promoted in_progress -> provenance_declared (nodejs.org/api, 20.19). 75 tests in test_javascript_module_completeness.py. The dual fs.open made javascript the third mode-decided language, and the parity test (test_io_mode_discrimination) refused it until the analyzer could produce the mode -- so the leg also shipped the javascript io_mode PRODUCER: _MODE_ARGUMENT_POSITIONS['javascript'] (flags at positional 1; typescript via the catalogue alias), stamp_io_mode_from_call reading string_fragment, js_ts.py stamping every emitted call; 22 tests in test_js_io_mode_emission.py (javascript + typescript).\n\nA/B (compare.py, old = dev 3a69d0bd1e catalogues, new = this branch; 11 javascript corpus repos, cold caches, claims NO-NET / NO-FSWRITE / NO-FSREAD / NO-SUBPROC): 0 of 44 verdict categories moved. Every surviving `inconclusive` is held by a rung the grants do not reach: a `console` method-shape withholding (express, ioredis, winston: the rows are `methods:` and the analyzer emits the calls without a method construct, so the coverage gate withholds while the classifier tags them — filed), and languages with no catalogue (vue, ruby, php/powershell, solidity — and `typescript` named as having none although it aliases javascript's, filed). The F7 deletion moved no NO-FSREAD verdict because every cohort repo reads files elsewhere. The positive control is the gate test: a call into a granted module now reaches `coverage.complete`, which no javascript call could before.\n\nRESIDUALS: WI-dovog-jikos-gijud-hukin-kohik-sihof-juvor-rusas (solidity-abi-linker's typescript-labelled synthetic srcs withhold every openzeppelin claim; WI-mital's family), WI-komun-lajas-hufuv-fuhoz-hipab-sabub-pijag-digoj (console/localStorage rows are `methods:` while named globals resolve function-shaped; the gate withholds what the classifier matched) -- the two rungs the A/B found holding every clean javascript verdict, placed before WI-dupok on the arc; WI-vihop-kimab-zovad-duzik-maduv-tonoj-nurol-zofoz (the `fs.promises.<fn>` member chain resolves to an untyped receiver and never reaches the rows; INV-linub's class, Phase 6). readline and http stay ungranted until the js io_target_kind stamp / constructor keying exist -- both are analyzer work, not catalogue work, and are named in the yaml."  # c81c
